1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,136
The decision was made in the basement of the lab, in a room with a mop in the corner and a full row of boxes on the shelf.

2
00:00:07,136 --> 00:00:13,131
“We begin with less and add more only when the term is clear,” Maya said.

3
00:00:13,131 --> 00:00:22,655
“That is the deal.” The board had asked for a second version, and the preparation for it took the whole summer.

4
00:00:22,655 --> 00:00:28,144
The technique was to cut the form at the centre and reduce it to one page.

5
00:00:28,144 --> 00:00:37,568
A guide for the staff, a layer of plain language over every field, and an exclusive cycle of review were the whole scheme.

6
00:00:37,568 --> 00:00:42,292
“Count the steps a person has to take,” she said.

7
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:46,682
“That number is the scale of our respect.”

8
00:00:46,682 --> 00:00:57,146
The smell of coffee and the smell of burnt dust came up from the pipes; the transmission of a report from the top floor was interrupted twice.

9
00:00:57,146 --> 00:01:04,205
“The trend is linear and the probability is not,” the analyst said, with caution.

10
00:01:04,205 --> 00:01:09,724
“A tremendous burst of enthusiasm is not continuity.”

11
00:01:09,724 --> 00:01:14,439
The justification for every line had to be written beside it.

12
00:01:14,439 --> 00:01:19,398
“Do not organize the fields by department,” Lin said.

13
00:01:19,398 --> 00:01:35,526
“Organize them by the question a person asks.” A roller of tape, a footprint of mud by the door, and a modifier that changed the meaning of a sentence: the details of a serious redesign.

14
00:01:35,526 --> 00:01:39,931
The jump from four fields to one was the hardest part.

15
00:01:39,931 --> 00:01:45,070
“We cannot interrupt the launch forever,” the director said.

16
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:56,744
“A board will not watch a disintegration in slow motion.” He was right, and the group had to put the decision in writing by the next session.

17
00:01:56,744 --> 00:02:05,268
The scene they agreed on was quiet: enter the room, look at the board, and start with the smallest version.

18
00:02:05,268 --> 00:02:11,897
If the nation wanted more, it would have to say so in the language of the form itself.

19
00:02:11,897 --> 00:02:26,305
The center of the argument was easy to see from the side of the room: the pattern would not change unless they intensified the pressure, and a large drop in the number of fields would include nothing but the essentials.

20
00:02:26,305 --> 00:02:29,825
A war of memos had already begun.

21
00:02:29,825 --> 00:02:36,322
The view from the basement was short, but the pattern was clear.
